                <pb facs="0258" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2028: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-09T18:00:00+01:00">October 9, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 9—3:48 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>168. Council meeting set for noon Tuesday, October 13, at Geneva. Drummond is
                    confident that Reading and Briand will attend and that other Foreign Ministers
                    will follow suit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
